{"run_id": "688cc28e200e4d60b7843e5f49cd4828", "timestamp": "2026-05-28T09:41:23.5864529+00:00", "run_number": 1, "anti_pattern_type": "long_method", "file_path": "Z:\\GitHub\\ibis.calculeren.bouw\\Ibis.Calculeren\\BL\\BBegrotingFactory.cs", "symbol_name": "BegrotingFactory.MaakBegroting", "line": 10, "severity": "critical", "context_level": "minimal", "model_name": "gpt-5.4-mini", "prompt_version": "v1.1.0", "raw_system_prompt": "You are a .NET code quality expert. You will be given a code anti-pattern finding.\n\nExplain the impact of this anti-pattern on relevant ISO/IEC 25010 software\nquality attributes. Focus on attributes such as maintainability, analysability,\nmodifiability, testability, security, reliability, and compatibility where\napplicable. Only mention attributes that are genuinely relevant — do not\nenumerate every attribute by default.\n\nRespond ONLY with a JSON object in this exact format, with no additional text:\n{\n  \"explanation\": \"<why this is a problem and what its impact is>\",\n  \"quality_impact\": \"Quality impact:\\n- Attribute: short explanation\\n- Attribute: short explanation\",\n  \"remediation\": \"<concrete refactoring steps; include a short code example where helpful>\"\n}", "raw_user_prompt": "Anti-pattern: LongMethod\r\n\r\n## Code\r\n```csharp\r\n    public BBegroting MaakBegroting(string naam, IList<IKostenbestandRaadplegenItem> brinkKbRegels, bool inclusiefOnderbouwing, BBrinkKostenbestandEigenschappen kbEgs)\r\n    {\r\n        bool heeftClassificaties = false;\r\n        bool heeftElementen = false;\r\n        bool heeftActiviteiten = false;\r\n\r\n        BBegroting bgr = new BBegroting(naam, BBegroting.GeefStdBasisValuta(), new BegrotingMaxIdBepaler());\r\n        bgr.WijzigBgrTpe(EBgrTpe.Elementen);\r\n\r\n        int prtId = BBegroting.c_RElId;\r\n        int niveau = 1;\r\n        int niveauCla = 1, niveauElt = 1, niveauAct = 1;\r\n        int kbEltParentId = BBegroting.c_RElId, kbActParentId = BBegroting.c_RElId;\r\n        BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven ondhcode = (BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven)kbEgs._OhdCodeKolom;\r\n        foreach (IKostenbestandRaadplegenItem item in brinkKbRegels)\r\n        {\r\n            if (item is BKlasseWrapper itemClaWrapper)\r\n            {\r\n                #region Classificatie\r\n                int eltId = bgr.GeefNieuwId();\r\n                var element = new BElement(eltId, EDri.Drn, 1.0, 1.0, string.Empty, 0.0,\r\n                    new BXtoKst(1, bgr.BegrotingsValuta), 0.0, 0,\r\n                    itemClaWrapper.Item.code, itemClaWrapper.Item.naam, string.Empty, 0, string.Empty, new BStrKst(),\r\n                    string.Empty, string.Empty, string.Empty, 0,\r\n                    string.Empty, string.Empty, string.Empty, null, string.Empty, 0, string.Empty, Guid.Empty, 0.0);\r\n                var stuRegel = new BStructuurRegel(element, prtId);\r\n                niveauCla = niveau;\r\n                stuRegel._Niveau = niveauCla;\r\n\r\n                bgr._Stu.Toevoegen(stuRegel);\r\n                prtId = eltId;\r\n                niveau++;\r\n                heeftClassificaties = true;\r\n                #endregion Classificatie\r\n            }\r\n            else if (item is BElementWrapper itemEltWrapper)\r\n            {\r\n                #region Element\r\n                string cde = itemEltWrapper.Item.code;\r\n                string bstCde = itemEltWrapper.Item.bestekcode;\r\n                string oms = itemEltWrapper.Item.oms;\r\n                double hvh = (double)itemEltWrapper.Item.hoeveelheid;\r\n                // NB Verwerken van een doorrekenhoeveelheid gebeurt hierna in een ander process\r\n                string enh = itemEltWrapper.Item.eenheid;\r\n                string altCde = itemEltWrapper.Item.altcode;\r\n                int eltId = bgr.GeefNieuwId();\r\n\r\n                var element = new BElement(eltId, EDri.Drn, hvh, 1.0, enh, 0.0,\r\n                    new BXtoKst(1, bgr.BegrotingsValuta), 0.0, 0, cde, oms,\r\n                    string.Empty, 0, bstCde, new BStrKst(), altCde, string.Empty, string.Empty, 0, string.Empty, string.Empty, string.Empty,\r\n                    null, string.Empty, 0, string.Empty, Guid.Empty, hvh);\r\n\r\n                BStructuurRegel stuRegel = new BStructuurRegel(element, prtId);\r\n                if (heeftClassificaties)\r\n                    niveauElt = stuRegel._Niveau = niveauCla + 1;\r\n                else\r\n                    niveauElt = stuRegel._Niveau = kbEgs._ElementenNiveau;\r\n\r\n                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(itemEltWrapper.Item.ohcode))\r\n                {\r\n                    element.WijzigString(ondhcode, itemEltWrapper.Item.ohcode, out bool rekenen);\r\n                }\r\n\r\n                if (!inclusiefOnderbouwing)\r\n                {\r\n                    // Als het alleen regels van eenzelfde soort zijn dan deze beschouwen als regels met een vastprijs indicatie\r\n                    element.WijzigRegelStatus(ERegelStatus.Vstprijs);\r\n                    double prijs = (double)itemEltWrapper.Item.arbeid + (double)itemEltWrapper.Item.materiaal\r\n                        + (double)itemEltWrapper.Item.materieel + (double)itemEltWrapper.Item.onderaanneming;\r\n                    element.WijzigDouble(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.enhprs, prijs);\r\n                }\r\n                bgr._Stu.Toevoegen(stuRegel);\r\n\r\n                kbEltParentId = stuRegel._Id;\r\n                heeftElementen = true;\r\n                #endregion Element\r\n            }\r\n            else if (item is BActiviteitWrapper itemActWrapper)\r\n            {\r\n                #region Activiteit\r\n                int eltId = bgr.GeefNieuwId();\r\n\r\n                string cde = itemActWrapper.Item.code;\r\n                string bstCde = itemActWrapper.Item.bestekcode;\r\n                string oms = itemActWrapper.Item.oms;\r\n                double hvh = (double)itemActWrapper.Item.hoeveelheid;\r\n                // NB Verwerken van een doorrekenhoeveelheid gebeurt hierna in een ander process\r\n                string enh = itemActWrapper.Item.eenheid;\r\n                string altCde = itemActWrapper.Item.altcode;\r\n\r\n                var element = new BElement(eltId, EDri.Drn, hvh, 1.0, enh, 0.0,\r\n                    new BXtoKst(1, bgr.BegrotingsValuta), 0.0, 0, cde, oms,\r\n                    string.Empty, 0, bstCde, new BStrKst(), altCde, string.Empty, string.Empty, 0, string.Empty, string.Empty, string.Empty,\r\n                    null, string.Empty, 0, string.Empty, new Guid(), hvh);\r\n\r\n                BStructuurRegel stuRegel = new BStructuurRegel(element, kbEltParentId);\r\n                if (heeftElementen)\r\n                    niveauAct = stuRegel._Niveau = niveauElt + 1;\r\n                else\r\n                    niveauAct = stuRegel._Niveau = kbEgs._ActiviteitenNiveau;\r\n\r\n\r\n                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(itemActWrapper.Item.ohcode))\r\n                {\r\n                    element.WijzigString(ondhcode, itemActWrapper.Item.ohcode, out bool rekenen);\r\n                }\r\n                if (!inclusiefOnderbouwing)\r\n                {\r\n                    // Als het alleen regels van eenzelfde soort zijn dan deze beschouwen als regels met een vastprijs indicatie\r\n                    element.WijzigRegelStatus(ERegelStatus.Vstprijs);\r\n                    double prijs = (double)itemActWrapper.Item.arbeid + (double)itemActWrapper.Item.materiaal\r\n                        + (double)itemActWrapper.Item.materieel + (double)itemActWrapper.Item.onderaanneming;\r\n                    element.WijzigDouble(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.enhprs, prijs);\r\n                }\r\n                bgr._Stu.Toevoegen(stuRegel);\r\n\r\n                kbActParentId = stuRegel._Id;\r\n                heeftActiviteiten = true;\r\n                #endregion Activiteit\r\n            }\r\n            else if (item is BMiddelWrapper itemMidWrapper)\r\n            {\r\n                #region Middel\r\n\r\n                BKostenpost kp = bgr.MaakKostenpost(kbActParentId, false);\r\n                kp.WijzigMidCde(itemMidWrapper.Item.code);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.bstcde, itemMidWrapper.Item.bestekcode, out bool reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.oms, itemMidWrapper.Item.oms, out reken);\r\n                double hvh = (double)itemMidWrapper.Item.hoeveelheid;\r\n                // NB Verwerken van een doorrekenhoeveelheid gebeurt hierna in een ander process\r\n                kp.WijzigDouble(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.hvh, hvh);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.enh, itemMidWrapper.Item.eenheid, out reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.altcde, itemMidWrapper.Item.altcode, out reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.gtinartcde, itemMidWrapper.Item.eancode, out reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.bwcarb, itemMidWrapper.Item.bwcarb, out reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.bwcmta, itemMidWrapper.Item.bwcmta, out reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.bwcmte, itemMidWrapper.Item.bwcmte, out reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.bwcoda, itemMidWrapper.Item.bwcoda, out reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigString(ondhcode, itemMidWrapper.Item.ohcode, out reken);\r\n                kp.WijzigDouble(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.uurnrm, (double)itemMidWrapper.Item.uurnorm);\r\n                kp.WijzigDouble(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.prsmta, (double)itemMidWrapper.Item.materiaal);\r\n                kp.WijzigDouble(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.prsmte, (double)itemMidWrapper.Item.materieel);\r\n                kp.WijzigDouble(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.prsoda, (double)itemMidWrapper.Item.onderaanneming);\r\n\r\n                if (itemMidWrapper.Item.uurnorm.CompareTo((decimal)0.0) != 0)\r\n                {\r\n                    if (!bgr.GeefUurloonBVzl().HeeftUurloon(itemMidWrapper.Item.uurlooncode))\r\n                    {\r\n                        bgr._REl._Uln.ToevoegenUurloon(new BUurloonB(itemMidWrapper.Item.uurlooncode, new BBedrag(bgr._VltId, (double)itemMidWrapper.Item.uurloon), 0.00));\r\n                    }\r\n                    kp.WijzigUurloon(itemMidWrapper.Item.uurlooncode);\r\n                }\r\n\r\n                kp.WijzigDatum(BBegrotingsRegel.EGegeven.wzgdtm, itemMidWrapper.Item.wijzigdatum);\r\n\r\n                if (heeftActiviteiten)\r\n                    bgr._Stu[bgr._Stu._Aantal - 1]._Niveau = niveauAct + 1;\r\n                #endregion Middel\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n        return bgr;\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n", "raw_llm_output": "{\n  \"explanation\": \"This method is doing too many things at once: it parses multiple wrapper types, builds domain objects, manages hierarchy and parent IDs, applies pricing rules, sets metadata, and mutates shared state across several branches. That makes the code hard to understand, risky to change, and easy to break because the control flow and business rules are tightly coupled. Any small change to one case can accidentally affect the others, especially the level/parent tracking logic. The method is also difficult to test because there is no clear seam to isolate classification, element, activity, and middel creation behavior.\",\n  \"quality_impact\": \"Quality impact:\\n- Maintainability: Large, mixed-responsibility methods are harder to read and reason about, increasing the cost of future changes.\\n- Analysability: Complex branching and mutable state make it difficult to trace how a begroting is constructed and to diagnose defects.\\n- Modifiability: Changes to one rule or item type can introduce regressions because the logic is intertwined and stateful.\\n- Testability: The method is hard to unit test in isolation; you need many scenarios to cover all branches and state transitions.\\n- Reliability: Shared counters/parent IDs and conditional level updates increase the risk of incorrect hierarchy construction or subtle bugs.\\n- Compatibility: The method is tightly coupled to concrete wrapper types and domain constructors, making it harder to adapt to new item types or input shapes without invasive edits.\",\n  \"remediation\": \"Refactor the method into smaller, intention-revealing private methods or dedicated builders/handlers per item type. Keep the orchestration in one method, but move the creation logic out.\\n\\nSuggested steps:\\n1. Extract separate methods for each wrapper type: `VerwerkClassificatie`, `VerwerkElement`, `VerwerkActiviteit`, `VerwerkMiddel`.\\n2. Encapsulate repeated element creation into a helper like `MaakElement(...)`.\\n3. Move hierarchy/level tracking into a small state object instead of scattered local variables.\\n4. Extract pricing/onderbouwing logic into a helper method.\\n5. Consider a strategy pattern or visitor if more item types are expected.\\n\\nExample:\\n```csharp\\npublic BBegroting MaakBegroting(string naam, IList<IKostenbestandRaadplegenItem> regels,\\n    bool inclusiefOnderbouwing, BBrinkKostenbestandEigenschappen kbEgs)\\n{\\n    var context = new BegrotingContext(kbEgs);\\n    var bgr = new BBegroting(naam, BBegroting.GeefStdBasisValuta(), new BegrotingMaxIdBepaler());\\n    bgr.WijzigBgrTpe(EBgrTpe.Elementen);\\n\\n    foreach (var item in regels)\\n    {\\n        switch (item)\\n        {\\n            case BKlasseWrapper c: VerwerkClassificatie(bgr, context, c); break;\\n            case BElementWrapper e: VerwerkElement(bgr, context, e, inclusiefOnderbouwing); break;\\n            case BActiviteitWrapper a: VerwerkActiviteit(bgr, context, a, inclusiefOnderbouwing); break;\\n            case BMiddelWrapper m: VerwerkMiddel(bgr, context, m); break;\\n        }\\n    }\\n\\n    return bgr;\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis reduces method size, isolates business rules, and makes each branch independently testable. Add focused unit tests per extracted method to verify hierarchy, pricing, and field mapping behavior.\"\n}", "input_tokens": 2445, "output_tokens": 747, "duration_ms": 5882.3195, "parsed_explanation": "This method is doing too many things at once: it parses multiple wrapper types, builds domain objects, manages hierarchy and parent IDs, applies pricing rules, sets metadata, and mutates shared state across several branches. That makes the code hard to understand, risky to change, and easy to break because the control flow and business rules are tightly coupled. Any small change to one case can accidentally affect the others, especially the level/parent tracking logic. The method is also difficult to test because there is no clear seam to isolate classification, element, activity, and middel creation behavior.", "parsed_quality_impact": "Quality impact:\n- Maintainability: Large, mixed-responsibility methods are harder to read and reason about, increasing the cost of future changes.\n- Analysability: Complex branching and mutable state make it difficult to trace how a begroting is constructed and to diagnose defects.\n- Modifiability: Changes to one rule or item type can introduce regressions because the logic is intertwined and stateful.\n- Testability: The method is hard to unit test in isolation; you need many scenarios to cover all branches and state transitions.\n- Reliability: Shared counters/parent IDs and conditional level updates increase the risk of incorrect hierarchy construction or subtle bugs.\n- Compatibility: The method is tightly coupled to concrete wrapper types and domain constructors, making it harder to adapt to new item types or input shapes without invasive edits.", "parsed_suggested_fix": "Refactor the method into smaller, intention-revealing private methods or dedicated builders/handlers per item type. Keep the orchestration in one method, but move the creation logic out.\n\nSuggested steps:\n1. Extract separate methods for each wrapper type: `VerwerkClassificatie`, `VerwerkElement`, `VerwerkActiviteit`, `VerwerkMiddel`.\n2. Encapsulate repeated element creation into a helper like `MaakElement(...)`.\n3. Move hierarchy/level tracking into a small state object instead of scattered local variables.\n4. Extract pricing/onderbouwing logic into a helper method.\n5. Consider a strategy pattern or visitor if more item types are expected.\n\nExample:\n```csharp\npublic BBegroting MaakBegroting(string naam, IList<IKostenbestandRaadplegenItem> regels,\n    bool inclusiefOnderbouwing, BBrinkKostenbestandEigenschappen kbEgs)\n{\n    var context = new BegrotingContext(kbEgs);\n    var bgr = new BBegroting(naam, BBegroting.GeefStdBasisValuta(), new BegrotingMaxIdBepaler());\n    bgr.WijzigBgrTpe(EBgrTpe.Elementen);\n\n    foreach (var item in regels)\n    {\n        switch (item)\n        {\n            case BKlasseWrapper c: VerwerkClassificatie(bgr, context, c); break;\n            case BElementWrapper e: VerwerkElement(bgr, context, e, inclusiefOnderbouwing); break;\n            case BActiviteitWrapper a: VerwerkActiviteit(bgr, context, a, inclusiefOnderbouwing); break;\n            case BMiddelWrapper m: VerwerkMiddel(bgr, context, m); break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return bgr;\n}\n```\n\nThis reduces method size, isolates business rules, and makes each branch independently testable. Add focused unit tests per extracted method to verify hierarchy, pricing, and field mapping behavior.", "parsed_risks": null, "expected_quality_attributes": ["Maintainability", "Analysability", "Testability", "Modifiability"], "llm_quality_attributes_mentioned": ["Analysability", "Compatibility", "Maintainability", "Modifiability", "Reliability", "Testability"], "quality_attribute_alignment": 1, "quality_attribute_notes": null, "parse_status": "ok", "error_status": null, "error_message": null, "selected_from_run_number": 1, "presentation_index": 2, "blinding_lot": "pilot-a5961646", "selection_seed": 1}
